### Process Submission from Blob Storage
POST http://localhost:7071/api/submissions/process
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "blobUrl": "https://example-storage.blob.core.windows.net/documents/sample-submission.xml",
  "fileName": "sample-submission.xml"
}

### Process Submission from Third-Party Blob (AWS S3 example)
POST http://localhost:7071/api/submissions/process
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "blobUrl": "https://my-bucket.s3.amazonaws.com/documents/submission-2024-01.xml",
  "fileName": "submission-2024-01.xml"
}

### Get Submission Status
GET http://localhost:7071/api/submissions/{{submissionId}}/status

### Get Submission Status History
GET http://localhost:7071/api/submissions/{{submissionId}}/status/history

### Get Communications for Submission
GET http://localhost:7071/api/submissions/{{submissionId}}/communications

### Example responses:

# Process Submission Response:
# {
#   "submissionId": "12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012",
#   "status": "Processing",
#   "isSuccess": true,
#   "startedAt": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z"
# }

# Submission Status Response:
# {
#   "id": "12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012",
